**The fix design (I have verified the mathematics and C-level behavior myself — implement exactly this):**

Replace the broken check with a **dual weighted mod-256 aggregate** (non-commutative mixing, per the report §2.1(iii)'s XOR-invariance theorem — pure-XOR mixing always cancels):

```
w1_i = 2*i + 1                      // 1,3,5,7,9,11,13,15 — pairwise distinct AND odd
w2_i = (2*i + 1) ^ 0x5A             // verified: still pairwise distinct and odd
W1 = (Σ_i w1_i * (data[i] + 1)) mod 256
W2 = (Σ_i w2_i * (data[i] + 1)) mod 256
```
- `tag()` snapshots W1, W2 (and drops the per-lane tag snapshot array entirely — it is provably inert).
- `verify()` recomputes both from the (possibly corrupted) data and mismatches if either differs.
- The `+1` term makes constant-data (e.g. all-zero data) produce a nonzero position-dependent sum, so all-same-byte data doesn't trivially collide.
